A permissions config. Every form here also runs in a session: one that tightens
the config takes effect at once and is saved with it, and one that loosens it
waits for the user's approval. In a file it is read as data, and anything
written outside a form is prose, like this paragraph.

What a call gets when no rule names it.

(permission/default allow)

Forms by name. A trailing star is a glob; a bare star is multiplication.

(permission/deny eval read :reason "no code built from strings")
(permission/ask memory/forget-all exit)

One MCP server. The names inside are its tool names, so this file never has to
spell github/ in front of each one.

(permission/server github
  (allow list_* get_* search_*)
  (ask create_* update_* merge_*)
  (deny delete_* :reason "nothing destructive on github")
  (hide admin_* *_token))

A server can show only what it names, and hide every other tool it has.

(permission/server playwright
  (only browser_navigate))

A whole server: denied stays discoverable and refuses to load, hidden is never
seen at all.

(permission/deny-server shell :reason "no shell access")
(permission/hide-server internal-metrics)

A single tool can be named from the top level too.

(permission/ask github/create_release)
